  "intro": "A proper rational function (numerator degree less than denominator) can be split into simpler fractions whose integrals are logs or arctangents. Factor the denominator; for distinct linear factors write $\\frac{A}{x-r_1}+\\frac{B}{x-r_2}+\\cdots$, clear denominators, and solve for the constants (plugging in the roots is quick). Repeated and irreducible quadratic factors need extra terms. If the fraction is improper, divide first.",
  "items": [
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 1,
      "prompt": "Decompose $\\dfrac{5x-1}{(x-1)(x+2)}$ into partial fractions.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Write $\\frac{5x-1}{(x-1)(x+2)}=\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{B}{x+2}$.",
          "Clear denominators: $5x-1=A(x+2)+B(x-1)$.",
          "Let $x=1$: $4=3A\\Rightarrow A=\\frac{4}{3}$. Let $x=-2$: $-11=-3B\\Rightarrow B=\\frac{11}{3}$.",
          "So it is $\\frac{4/3}{x-1}+\\frac{11/3}{x+2}$."
        ],
        "answer": "$\\dfrac{4/3}{x-1}+\\dfrac{11/3}{x+2}$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 2,
      "prompt": "Evaluate $\\int \\dfrac{1}{(x-1)(x+1)}\\,dx$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Decompose: $\\frac{1}{(x-1)(x+1)}=\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{B}{x+1}$ with $1=A(x+1)+B(x-1)$.",
          "Let $x=1$: $1=2A\\Rightarrow A=\\frac{1}{2}$; let $x=-1$: $1=-2B\\Rightarrow B=-\\frac{1}{2}$.",
          "Integrate: $\\frac{1}{2}\\ln|x-1|-\\frac{1}{2}\\ln|x+1|+C$."
        ],
        "answer": "$\\dfrac{1}{2}\\ln\\left|\\dfrac{x-1}{x+1}\\right|+C$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 3,
      "prompt": "Evaluate $\\int \\dfrac{3}{x^2-9}\\,dx$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Factor: $x^2-9=(x-3)(x+3)$; decompose $\\frac{3}{(x-3)(x+3)}=\\frac{A}{x-3}+\\frac{B}{x+3}$.",
          "$3=A(x+3)+B(x-3)$: $x=3$ gives $A=\\frac{1}{2}$, $x=-3$ gives $B=-\\frac{1}{2}$.",
          "Integrate: $\\frac{1}{2}\\ln|x-3|-\\frac{1}{2}\\ln|x+3|+C$."
        ],
        "answer": "$\\dfrac{1}{2}\\ln\\left|\\dfrac{x-3}{x+3}\\right|+C$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
